            <div xml:id="d598">

                <pb facs="0705" n="585" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg585"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.24/145a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lay</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-01-30T16:00:00-05:00">January 30, 1931—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>8.… has submitted to the Department an application for license to export to the
                    Government of Honduras 280,000 thirty-eight caliber <pb facs="0706" n="586"
                        xml:id="pg586"/> cartridges and 120,000 thirty-two caliber cartridges.
                    Because of the calibers specified the Department desires you to ascertain and
                    report by telegraph whether this material would be imported strictly for
                    Government use.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
